      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before Stone County’s first court met in Jamestown, Cape Fair hosted the county’s inaugural court sessions in John B.’s home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cape_fair_missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cape Fair sits on the west side of the James River arm of Table Rock Lake, placing it right beside Missouri’s largest reservoir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Fair%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cape Fair is included in the Branson Micropolitan Statistical Area, linking it economically to the regional tourism hub.",
